<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Vision wins A$9.5 mln navy contract.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Vision wins A$9.5 mln navy contract.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Technology company Vision Systems Ltd said on Friday its subsidiary Vision Abell Pty Ltd had signed a A$9.5 million contract with the Australian Defence Department to develop a generic threat simulator (GTS).</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the GTS concept demonstrator would be used by the Royal Australian Navy in tests and training for its Nulka active missile decoy system, a hovering rocket which decoys incoming missiles away from ships.</p>
<p>Work on the contract would begin immediately, with full acceptance scheduled for October 1, 1998, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
